[{"category":"section","location":"#SampledDomains","page":"Home","text":"","title":"SampledDomains"},{"category":"module","location":"#SampledDomains.SampledDomains","page":"Home","text":"The goal of the module is to attach physical coordinates to array elements, so a[i,j] could be interpreted as f(x_i y_j) for some function f.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SampledDomains.SampledDomains"},{"category":"type","location":"#SampledDomains.SampledDomain","page":"Home","text":"SampledDomain(vals::Array, dom::AbstractDomain)\nSampledDomain(f::Function, dom::AbstractDomain)\n\nContains two fileds: vals and dom representing sampled values of function f on domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SampledDomains.SampledDomain"},{"category":"function","location":"#SampledDomains.dualRange","page":"Home","text":"dualRange(xrange::AbstractRange, q::Int =1)\n\nConstruct range in Fourier-transform-dual domain with upsampling factor q. If sampling in x has step size Δx, the dual domain is sampled in interval (-q/2Δx, q/2Δx).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SampledDomains.dualRange"}]
